{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 8: beliefs about demand. Demand grows for 25 weeks and then levels off; three planners form expectations in different ways. }
Base Demand=
	100
	~	cases/week
	~	Demand before growth starts.
	|
Growth=
	2
	~	cases/week/week
	~	Weekly increase in demand while the market grows.
	|
Growth Start=
	5
	~	week
	~	When demand starts to grow.
	|
Growth End=
	30
	~	week
	~	When demand stops growing.
	|
Demand=
	Base Demand + RAMP(Growth, Growth Start, Growth End)
	~	cases/week
	~	Customer demand.
	|
Averaging Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	Time over which planners average demand.
	|
Forecast Horizon=
	4
	~	week
	~	How far ahead the trend-following planner projects.
	|
Adaptive Belief=
	SMOOTH(Demand, Averaging Time)
	~	cases/week
	~	Exponential smoothing: adaptive expectations.
	|
Adaptive Belief 3=
	SMOOTH3(Demand, Averaging Time)
	~	cases/week
	~	Third-order smoothing with the same average delay.
	|
Perceived Trend=
	TREND(Demand, Averaging Time, 0)
	~	1/week
	~	Fractional growth the planner believes in.
	|
Extrapolative Belief=
	FORECAST(Demand, Averaging Time, Forecast Horizon)
	~	cases/week
	~	Demand now projected ahead at the perceived trend.
	|
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ week ~ |
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = TIME STEP ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
